																		Attribution, Thanks and Other Matters
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2039383&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608475951" alt="MrWrong" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2039383)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;" >MrWrong</a></span> <span class="odate time_1464486960 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 May 2016 01:56</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2516007">
									

<p>This was inspired Aoneareyou60 of reddit, who issued a prompt on &quot;Roadkill Revenge&quot; here ://www.reddit.com/r/SCP/comments/4kpv98/another_scp_idea_roadkill_revenge/</p>
<p>I did modify the initial prompt heavily since then&#8230;</p>
<p>Thank you to reviewers such as Hercules Rockefeller, Scorpion451, Steeltitan, Moen and others.</p>
<p>This article features the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>SCP-2372 (Soulmates) by MrWrong</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So this SCP somehow ended up in my re-using &quot;Old Chin&quot;, a character mentioned in SCP-2372. I think it is befitting, as both SCPs deal with Chinese supernatural elements to some extent.</p>
<p>The LTE-1985-Grey Bluechild are reminiscent of Chiyou's followers as described in <a href="/document-2481">Document-2481</a>, who essentially sided with the Brass Dragon and gained bodies of metal.</p>
<p>The road here is a residue of different thaumaturgies mixed onto one place, the Taoist-style reanimation and Brass Dragon's blessings.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

